From 2a2f085dc1f920cabf8b8bc18686b9f974b27dac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shae Wilde <shaecodes@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:53:49 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7921: extend injected legacy rate fix to
 MT7920/MT7921

Independent testing of the cleaned MT7922 patch on MT7921 PCIe 14c3:7961
succeeded in both directions on channel 44 after removing the model
guard. Only mt7921e was rebuilt; the other mt76 components stayed stock.

Include MT7921 (chip ID 0x7961) and MT7920 in the existing PCI rate
preservation path. Keep MT7902, which also uses this driver, outside the
scope of this revision. MT7920 shares the preparation path but has not
been tested on hardware.

Keep the existing band/rate validation, HT/VHT and encapsulation
exclusions, flag restoration, ACK policy, and common antenna/SPE setup.

This is a follow-up to the unreleased fork patch 02b6c9a1. A cumulative
upstream submission needs a revised description and a verified earliest
Fixes reference; the original MT7922 support tag alone does not describe
the newly reported MT7921 failure.

Link: https://github.com/t4t5/omdrop-owl/issues/14#issuecomment-6177921979
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-6.1-sol [exec_command]
---
 mt7921/pci_mac.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mt7921/pci_mac.c b/mt7921/pci_mac.c
index 5fb9a28c2..c91163dc4 100644
--- a/mt7921/pci_mac.c
+++ b/mt7921/pci_mac.c
@@ -44,7 +44,7 @@ int mt7921e_tx_prepare_skb(struct mt76_dev *mdev, void *txwi_ptr,
 	}
 
 	/* Save the rate before TX status bookkeeping clears control.flags. */
-	if (is_mt7922(mdev) &&
+	if ((mt76_chip(mdev) == 0x7961 || is_mt7920(mdev) || is_mt7922(mdev)) &&
 	    !(info->flags & IEEE80211_TX_CTL_HW_80211_ENCAP) &&
 	    (info->flags & IEEE80211_TX_CTL_INJECTED) &&
 	    (info->control.flags & IEEE80211_TX_CTRL_RATE_INJECT) &&
